Subject: [PATCH 20/69] fix(cli): use display_messages() in streaming paths to
 match message list (#130)

* fix(cli): use display_messages() in streaming paths to match message list

The stream_messages (polling) and subscribe_and_stream (push) paths
were iterating raw room_state.recent_messages.messages, which includes
action messages (edits, deletions, reactions) that the UI and
`riverctl message list` filter out via display_messages(). This caused
the CLI streaming commands to show different authors/messages than
the UI for the same room.

All three CLI message display paths now use display_messages() which
filters out action and deleted messages, matching the UI behavior.

For the subscription path, the delta and full-state update handlers
are unified: on any update notification, the merged room state is
fetched and display_messages() is used, which also simplifies the code.

Closes #122

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* refactor: simplify take-last-N pattern, restore delta optimization

Address code review feedback:
- Replace verbose triple-collect iterator chain with slice indexing
- Restore separate delta/state arms in subscribe handler: only fetch
  room state when a new displayable message is found in the delta,
  avoiding unnecessary network calls on every notification

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

